# Maintained by ARPA-H. Every path requires review from a listed owner via
# the `main` Ruleset's "require code owner review" rule - GitHub enforces
# this server-side against live review state, so it cannot be forged or
# staled by any workflow.
#
# IMPORTANT: CODEOWNERS fails OPEN on invalid entries (unknown users/teams
# are silently ignored, and a file with no valid owners satisfies the rule
# vacuously - exactly what happened with the inherited upstream Zendesk
# teams this file used to name). The "CODEOWNERS validity" workflow calls
# GitHub's codeowners/errors API on every PR and fails on any error, so a
# typo or a departed account can never silently disable review enforcement
# again. Owners must have write access to count.

